      "title": "Replica convergence",
      "description": "Lamport clocks and live vertex counts per site. Converged replicas hold the same vertex count and stop advancing their clocks \u2014 a clock that climbs while nothing changes means writes are not content-addressed and anti-entropy will never settle.",
